.page return 1 leave a shell function

# SYNOPSIS
*return* [_STATUS_]

# DESCRIPTION
`return` is a gapsh builtin that ends the current function, or a script run with `source`, with the given status (the status of the last command by default).

# EXAMPLES
    isdir() { [ -d "$1" ] && return 0; return 1; }

# SEE ALSO
exit(1), local(1), gapsh-language(7)
